---
import Layout from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Layout.astro';
import Journey from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Journey.astro';
import InvestorDeck from '../../smarttec-investor/components/InvestorDeck.astro';
import CinematicArt from '../../components/CinematicArt.astro';
import '../../styles/cinematic-investor.css';
import BrandLockup from '../../components/BrandLockup.astro';
import {pageAccess,privateHeaders} from '../../smarttec-investor/server/auth.mjs';
import CampusPreview from '../../components/CampusPreview.astro';
import {model,base,contracted,maximum,headlineIrr,assumptions as a,usd,rate,pct,millions,serviceLines,evidence} from '../../smarttec-investor/financial-model.mjs';
import {currentInvestmentFacts} from '../../smarttec-investor/current-facts.mjs';
export const prerender=false;
Object.entries(privateHeaders).forEach(([k,v])=>Astro.response.headers.set(k,v));
const access=await pageAccess(Astro.request);
if(access.error)return new Response('Private access is temporarily unavailable.',{status:503,headers:privateHeaders});
if(!access.session)return new Response(null,{status:303,headers:{...privateHeaders,Location:'/investors/login'}});
const phaseOneScenarios=model.scenarios.filter(s=>s.id!=='maximum-base');
const baseYear2=base.annual.find(y=>y.year===2)!;
const allBaseOperatingYearsPositive=base.annual.every(y=>y.operatingCashUsd>0);
const downside=model.scenarios.find(s=>s.id==='downside')!;
const infrastructureLabels:Record<string,string>={'Electrical distribution from the 3,000A main':'Electrical distribution allowance','Daikin Trailblazer chillers, installed (incl. spare)':'Two nominal 50-ton chillers, installed allowance','Contingency (things we haven\'t thought of)':'Contingency'};
---
<Layout>
<a href="#opportunity" class="inv-skip">Skip to content</a><Journey />
<main id="inv-main" data-model-version={model.version} data-model-source={model.source.sha256}>
<section id="opportunity" class="inv-hero inv-section">
<CinematicArt path="/investors" instance="investment" />
<div class="inv-hero-copy"><p class="inv-eyebrow">MEAD, OKLAHOMA / DEVELOPMENT STAGE</p>
<h1>Compute with a plan.<br/><em>Customers before scale.</em></h1>
<p class="inv-lead">A proposed {base.capacity.installedGpus}-B300 first fleet. Grid power at launch. Shared inference and dedicated GPU servers, alongside separately scoped colocation. Investment depends on documented customer economics and a fully commissioned facility.</p>
<div class="inv-actions"><a href="/investors/pitch" class="inv-button" data-pitch-launch>Open immersive investor deck ↗</a><a href="/investors/presentation" class="inv-outline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View investor PDF ↗</a><a href="#returns" class="inv-outline">Review model v{model.version} ↓</a></div>
<p class="inv-note">Customer discussions are active; no signed customer contract or paid pilot is established. All contracted returns below are hypothetical.</p></div>
<div class="inv-hero-bottom"><span>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/><small>CONCEPT ART / NOT INSTALLED EQUIPMENT</small></span><span>PROPOSED FIRST DEPLOYMENT<br/><strong>8 systems / 64 B300 GPUs / 60 saleable</strong></span></div>
</section>
<InvestorDeck />
<section id="deployment" class="inv-section">
<p class="inv-eyebrow">01 / THE SERVICE MODEL</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Two compute offerings.<br/>A separate colocation service.</h2><p>Shared inference and dedicated servers use SmartTec-owned hardware. Colocation houses customer-owned equipment. Model v{model.version} covers the owned B300 fleet; it does not add colocation, manufacturing or future energy-project revenue.</p></div>
<div class="inv-three-col">{serviceLines.map((s,i)=><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">0{i+1} / {s.tenancy}</p><h3>{s.name}</h3><p>{s.description}</p><small>{s.ownership}</small></article>)}</div>
<div class="inv-stat-row"><div><strong>{base.capacity.nodes}</strong><span>Complete systems proposed</span></div><div><strong>{base.capacity.installedGpus}</strong><span>GPUs in the purchase model</span></div><div><strong>{base.capacity.saleableGpus}</strong><span>Saleable GPU allocation</span></div><div><strong>{base.capacity.heldBackGpus}</strong><span>Held back from billing</span></div></div>
<p class="inv-note">Four held-back GPUs are a financial allocation, not a spare eight-GPU system or proven failover. Full-node dedicated bookings and shared capacity must fit one inventory; neither GPU-hours nor facility power can be sold twice. The campus concept now uses direct liquid cooling; exact Supermicro SKU and customer isolation requirements remain subject to vendor and engineering confirmation. Model v{model.version} retains the earlier air-cooled budget and requires repricing for the newer design.</p>
</section>
<section id="capital" class="inv-section inv-light">
<p class="inv-eyebrow">02 / INITIAL CAPITAL</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>A complete model.<br/>A budget to validate.</h2><p>Base initial funding is {usd(base.capital.totalUsd)}. This is the exact upgraded workbook total for eight systems, infrastructure and opening working cash. It remains a planning allowance pending firm procurement, utility and installation scopes.</p></div>
<div class="inv-three-col"><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">BASE INITIAL FUNDING</p><h3 class="inv-number">{millions(base.capital.totalUsd)}</h3><p>Hardware, infrastructure and working cash. All equipment is funded at inception; no debt is assumed.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">FOUNDER FUNDS REPORTED</p><h3 class="inv-number">{millions(a.initialFounderCapitalUsd)}</h3><p>Management reports funds available and willingness to cover overage. Availability, transfers and contribution terms remain unverified.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">BASE OVERAGE</p><h3 class="inv-number">{usd(base.capital.founderFundingGapUsd)}</h3><p>Above reported founder funds. This is a model gap, not an agreed external raise or investment offering.</p></article></div>
<div class="v61-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Base capital breakdown"><table><caption>Base initial funding · USD · planning allowances</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Use of funds</th><th scope="col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">8 complete B300 systems × {usd(base.capital.nodePriceUsd)}</th><td>{usd(base.capital.serverHardwareUsd)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shared storage and spares</th><td>{usd(base.capital.storageAndSparesUsd)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Freight and tax allowance</th><td>{usd(base.capital.freightAndTaxUsd)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Infrastructure including contingency</th><td>{usd(base.capital.infrastructureUsd)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Opening working cash: reserve and receivables</th><td>{usd(base.capital.cashReserveUsd)}</td></tr><tr class="v61-total"><th scope="row">Total modeled initial funding</th><td>{usd(base.capital.totalUsd)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<details class="inv-details"><summary>Infrastructure scope and allowances</summary><div class="v61-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Infrastructure allowance detail"><table><caption>Included within {usd(base.capital.infrastructureUsd)} infrastructure</caption><tbody>{base.capital.infrastructureBreakdown.map(item=><tr><th scope="row">{infrastructureLabels[item.label]||item.label}</th><td>{usd(item.amountUsd)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="inv-note">The generator allowance covers a docking station, not an installed or fuelled standby generator. Utility transformer/service upgrades, voltage compatibility, final equipment performance and complete installation must be reconciled against these allowances before commitment.</p></details>
<p class="inv-note">Model reserve: {a.cashReserveMonths} months of operating costs plus receivables at inception. A retained-cash target controls annual distributions; it is not an enforced minimum balance or proof that every month is funded. Values display rounded to whole dollars; the downloadable snapshot retains full precision.</p>
</section>
<section id="returns" class="inv-section inv-machine">
<p class="inv-eyebrow">03 / REVIEWED MODEL v{model.version}</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Cash-positive operations.<br/>Capital return below the hurdle.</h2><p>The Base model produces positive annual operating cash, but its five-year headline project IRR remains below the {pct(a.hurdleRate,0)} underwriting hurdle. Stronger customer terms or lower delivered cost must be documented before the model becomes an investable return case.</p></div>
<div class="v61-return-pair"><article><span>Base Year 2 · operating project cash</span><strong>{millions(baseYear2.operatingCashUsd)}</strong><p>{allBaseOperatingYearsPositive?'Every modeled Base year has positive operating cash.':'Operating cash varies by year.'} Year 2 gross revenue is {millions(baseYear2.revenueUsd)} and EBITDA is {millions(baseYear2.ebitdaUsd)}. This cash is before any outside-investor ownership or waterfall.</p></article><article><span>Base · five-year headline project IRR</span><strong class="v61-negative">{pct(headlineIrr(base))}</strong><p>Includes the workbook's annual operating project cash, reserve release and terminal recovery. Headline NPV at the {pct(a.hurdleRate,0)} hurdle is {usd(base.returns.npvUsd)}; operating capital payback is not reached within the hold.</p></article></div>
<p class="inv-note">Positive operating cash does not by itself repay the initial {usd(base.capital.totalUsd)}. Base operating cash leaves {usd(base.returns.unrecoveredOperatingCapitalUsd)} unrecovered at the end of the modeled hold before terminal recovery. Project results include modeled tax and BC LLC payments, but they do not establish an investor ownership share, waterfall or promised return. Annual-funded IRR and dated-funded XIRR remain timing diagnostics.</p>
<div class="v61-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Reviewed scenario comparison"><table><caption>Workbook selector cases · all customer contract inputs remain unsigned · USD</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Scenario</th><th scope="col">Initial funding</th><th scope="col">Year 2 operating cash</th><th scope="col">Headline project IRR</th><th scope="col">NPV at 15%</th><th scope="col">Operating payback</th></tr></thead><tbody>{model.scenarios.map(s=><tr><th scope="row">{s.label}<small>{s.capacity.installedGpus} installed / {s.capacity.saleableGpus} saleable · {s.commercial.buildMonths} build months</small></th><td>{usd(s.capital.totalUsd)}</td><td>{usd(s.annual.find(y=>y.year===2)?.operatingCashUsd||0)}</td><td class:list={[headlineIrr(s)<a.hurdleRate&&'v61-caution']}>{pct(headlineIrr(s))}</td><td>{usd(s.returns.npvUsd)}</td><td>{s.returns.operatingPaybackYears===null?`Not reached; ${usd(s.returns.unrecoveredOperatingCapitalUsd)} unrecovered`:s.returns.operatingPaybackYears.toFixed(2)+' years'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="inv-note">None of the six Phase-1 selector cases clears the {pct(a.hurdleRate,0)} hurdle in this workbook. The separate maximum-size Base sensitivity models {maximum.capacity.installedGpus} installed / {maximum.capacity.saleableGpus} saleable GPUs and a {pct(headlineIrr(maximum))} headline IRR; it is not an approved expansion. The delayed-customer case assumes {model.scenarios.find(s=>s.id==='delayed')!.commercial.buildMonths} build months.</p>
<details class="inv-details" open><summary>Commercial assumptions behind every comparison</summary><div class="v61-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Commercial assumptions"><table><caption>Rates and utilization are model inputs, not public offers, measured demand or signed prices</caption><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Customer contract input</th><th>Merchant pricing</th><th>Merchant paid utilization</th></tr></thead><tbody>{phaseOneScenarios.map(s=><tr><th scope="row">{s.label}</th><td>{s.commercial.contractedGpus?`${s.commercial.contractedGpus} GPUs · ${rate(s.commercial.contractRateUsd)}/GPU-hour · ${pct(s.commercial.contractPaidShare,0)} paid · ${s.commercial.contractTermMonths} months`:'No signed or modeled fixed customer block'}</td><td>{rate(s.commercial.merchantRateYear1Usd)} Year-1 reference · {pct(s.commercial.annualMerchantRateChange,0)} annually</td><td>{pct(s.commercial.merchantUtilizationYear1,0)} Year 1 · {pct(s.commercial.merchantUtilizationYear2Plus,0)} thereafter</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="inv-note">The Contracted selector case assumes {contracted.commercial.contractedGpus} GPUs at {rate(contracted.commercial.contractRateUsd)} per GPU-hour, {pct(contracted.commercial.contractPaidShare,0)} paid share and a {contracted.commercial.contractTermMonths}-month term. The remaining saleable fleet follows that case's merchant inputs. Paid contract hours are a minimum-payment assumption, not observed utilization or secured demand. Dedicated whole-server pricing must reconcile to the underlying GPU-hour budget.</p></details>
<div class="inv-three-col v61-assumptions"><article><h3>Operating costs</h3><p>Grid energy {(a.energyUsdPerKwh*100).toFixed(1)}¢/kWh plus {usd(a.demandUsdPerKwMonth)}/billed kW/month. Model average PUE {a.averagePue}; cost inflation {pct(a.annualCostInflation,0)}. The Phase-1 internet allowance is $4,000/month; it is not a confirmed carrier package. Staffing, insurance, support and channel fees are included.</p></article><article><h3>Cash and tax</h3><p>{pct(a.taxRate,0)} modeled tax; BC LLC receives {pct(a.bcLlcShare,0)} of positive after-tax accounting income. Net-{a.collectionDays} collection. Annual distributions retain a cost-reserve target. Tax treatment and site-agreement wording require professional review.</p></article><article><h3>Exit and service</h3><p>Hardware resale: {pct(a.hardwareResaleYear5,0)} in Year 5 / {pct(a.hardwareResaleYear6,0)} in Year 6. Infrastructure recovery: {pct(a.infrastructureResale,0)}. Included support: {a.includedSupportMonths} months from first billing, then {pct(a.postWarrantySupportRate,0)} of B300 system purchase cost annually before escalation. No buyback or service-term assurance.</p></article></div>
{model.scenarios.map(s=><details class="inv-details"><summary>{s.label} — annual cash-flow detail</summary><div class="v61-table inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label={s.label+' annual cash flows'}><table><caption>Initial contribution {usd(s.capital.totalUsd)} · gross billing differs from cash receipts · USD</caption><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Operating months</th><th>Gross revenue</th><th>Opex incl. fees</th><th>EBITDA</th><th>Operating project cash after tax / site share</th><th>Modeled distribution</th></tr></thead><tbody>{s.annual.map(y=><tr><th scope="row">{y.year}</th><td>{y.operatingMonths}</td><td>{usd(y.revenueUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.opexUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.ebitdaUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.operatingCashUsd)}</td><td>{usd(y.distributionsUsd)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="inv-note">Headline project IRR: {pct(headlineIrr(s))}; headline NPV at {pct(a.hurdleRate,0)}: {usd(s.returns.npvUsd)}; headline MOIC: {s.returns.moic.toFixed(3)}×. Separate post-sale receivable collection: {usd(s.returns.terminalReceivableUsd)}. Modeled distributions include working-cash timing. Separate net asset-sale cash at exit: {usd(s.annual.reduce((total,y)=>total+y.resaleUsd+y.resaleTaxUsd,0))}. Operating-only IRR, excluding terminal recovery: {pct(s.returns.operatingOnlyIrr)}. Operating capital payback: {s.returns.operatingPaybackYears===null?`not reached within the hold; ${usd(s.returns.unrecoveredOperatingCapitalUsd)} remains unrecovered`:s.returns.operatingPaybackYears.toFixed(2)+' modeled years (annual interpolation, not a guaranteed date)'}.</p></details>)}
<div class="inv-actions"><a class="inv-button" href="/api/investor/model" download="SmartTec_Model_v6.1_1_Verified_Scenarios.json">Download verified model snapshot ↓</a><a class="inv-outline" href="/investors/presentation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the PDF analysis ↗</a></div>
<details class="inv-details"><summary>Methodology, source and limits</summary><p>Model v{model.version}, reviewed {model.reviewedAt}. The authoritative workbook contains {model.source.formulaCount.toLocaleString('en-US')} formulas. The six Phase-1 selector cases and maximum-size Base sensitivity were recalculated in native Excel from disposable copies and independently checked for capital, revenue, cash, NPV and returns; the supplied source file remained unchanged.</p><p>Source: {model.source.filename}</p><p class="v61-hash">SHA-256: {model.source.sha256}</p><p>Headline project IRR is the workbook's quoted return metric. Annual-funded IRR and dated-funded XIRR are diagnostics for cash-distribution timing. The {a.modelStartDate} start date is a placeholder used for dated-return calculations; it is not a service-availability commitment. The workbook contains a 24-month launch cash view, but the full hold remains an annual distribution model. The Downside case requires a later modeled contribution of {usd(downside.returns.laterCapitalCallsUsd)}; the other published cases do not. This annual model does not prove continuous liquidity, absence of default or protection against unbudgeted cost.</p></details>
</section>
<CampusPreview id="campus" investor />

<section id="evidence" class="inv-section inv-light"><p class="inv-eyebrow">04 / EXECUTION AND EVIDENCE</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Clear assumptions.<br/>Defined release gates.</h2><p>A checked spreadsheet establishes arithmetic under its assumptions. Customer contracts, vendor documents and commissioned performance establish a business that can deliver them.</p></div><div class="inv-evidence">{evidence.map(item=><div><strong>{item.title}</strong><span><b>{item.status}.</b> {item.detail}</span></div>)}</div>
<details class="inv-details"><summary>Engineering assumptions in the first-phase budget</summary><p>{base.technical.itKw.toFixed(1)} kW total IT load; {base.technical.facilityPeakKw.toFixed(1)} kW modeled worst-day facility load; {base.technical.billedPeakKw.toFixed(1)} kW billed-demand assumption. Thermal duty is {base.technical.coolingLoadTons.toFixed(2)} tons. Two nominal {base.technical.chillerUnitTons}-ton chillers and {base.technical.inRowCoolerCount} × {base.technical.inRowUnitKw}-kW in-row units include spare units; installed nominal capacity is not usable redundant capacity.</p><p>The chiller screen uses {pct(base.technical.designChillerCapacityFactor,0)} capacity at design conditions, leaving only {pct(base.technical.nPlusOneChillerMargin,1)} modeled margin with one chiller out. Manufacturer derating, voltage, hydraulic layout and residual heat require design confirmation. The {base.technical.serviceVoltage} V / {base.technical.serviceAmps.toLocaleString('en-US')} A input is a planning service basis, not proof that the selected server and cooling equipment can connect directly.</p></details>
<ol class="v61-gates"><li>Execute customer minimum-payment and acceptance terms with credit support.</li><li>Confirm exact OEM configuration, utility tariff/capacity and complete contractor scope.</li><li>Document founder contributions, site rights and any investor security terms.</li><li>Complete commissioning, failover and workload acceptance before customer service.</li></ol></section>
<section id="questions" class="inv-section"><p class="inv-eyebrow">05 / PROJECT RECORDS</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Answers with context.</h2><p>Explore the reviewed model and management statements. Unverified items remain identified.</p></div><p id="inv-app-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Connecting to private project records…</p><form id="inv-question-form" class="inv-question-form"><label for="inv-question">Your question</label><div class="inv-login-row"><input id="inv-question" placeholder="What is included in the initial funding?" minlength="3" maxlength="1000" required/><button class="inv-button" type="submit" disabled>Find an answer</button></div></form><div id="inv-answer" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="inv-faq-list">{currentInvestmentFacts.map(f=><details class="inv-details"><summary>{f.question}</summary><p>{f.answer}</p><p class="inv-note">{f.status} · Reviewed {f.reviewedAt}</p></details>)}</div></section>
</main><footer class="inv-footer"><BrandLockup /><p>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/>Development stage · Model v{model.version} · {model.reviewedAt}</p><a href="mailto:yasir@smarttec.dev?subject=SmartTec%20investment%20discussion">Arrange a discussion</a><p class="inv-note">Private planning information. Financial projections are conditional model results. Customer commitments, installed costs, site rights, funding and investor terms require documentation.</p></footer>
</Layout>
<script>import '../../smarttec-investor/client/app.mjs';</script>
<style>
.v61-return-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;margin:3rem 0}.v61-return-pair article{padding:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,3rem);border:1px solid #aacbb447;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(140deg,#071e17b0,#31624a40)}.v61-return-pair article>span{font:12px/1.6 var(--f-mono);color:#cde2d3}.v61-return-pair strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(3.5rem,7vw,6.5rem);font-weight:500;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:1rem 0;color:#98edac}.v61-return-pair .v61-negative{color:#ffc5a5}.v61-return-pair p{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.6}.v61-table{max-height:none;margin:2rem 0}.v61-table table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;min-width:640px}.v61-table th,.v61-table td{text-align:left;padding:1rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid #a7b9ad55;vertical-align:top;white-space:normal}.v61-table th{font-weight:500}.v61-table thead th{font:11px/1.5 var(--f-mono);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}.v61-table caption{text-align:left;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;padding:1rem 0;color:inherit}.v61-table th small{display:block;min-width:190px;font-weight:400;opacity:.8;font-size:.78rem;margin-top:.5rem}.v61-table .v61-total{font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:600}.v61-caution{color:#ffc5a5}.v61-hash{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:12px/1.7 var(--f-mono)}.v61-assumptions{margin:3rem 0}.v61-assumptions article{padding-right:1.5rem}.v61-gates{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:75ch;padding-left:1.3rem;margin-top:3rem}.inv-hero-copy .inv-note{max-width:70ch}.inv-evidence>div{grid-template-columns:1fr 3fr}.inv-evidence b{font-weight:500}.inv-number{overflow-wrap:anywhere}#capital .v61-table table{min-width:0}#capital .v61-table td{width:35%;white-space:nowrap;text-align:right}.v61-table::-webkit-scrollbar{height:8px}.v61-table::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:#6e987c;border-radius:6px}
@media(max-width:760px){#returns .v61-table::before{content:"Swipe horizontally to see all columns →";display:block;position:sticky;left:0;width:calc(100vw - 12vw);font:11px/1.6 var(--f-mono);color:#b5e7c4;padding:.6rem 0}#capital .v61-table th,#capital .v61-table td{padding:.9rem .35rem;font-size:.9rem}.v61-return-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.v61-table{margin:1.5rem 0}.inv-evidence>div{grid-template-columns:1fr}.v61-return-pair strong{font-size:4rem}}
</style>
